{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And his anger burned.</b> Because she was indignant that he had brought her a Hebrew man to mock her — for in truth his anger did not burn against Joseph in this matter, since he believed Joseph's words more, but he placed him in the prison house in order to show that he believed her, for her honor; and he made use of Joseph in the prison house, as it says: וַיִּפְקֹד שַׂר הַטַּבָּחִים אֶת יוֹסֵף אִתָּם (Genesis 40:4)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:58.183457684Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}